  body: "# Causation and evidence for a trade-dispute decision\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    guidance requires the relevant place of employment, dispute, stoppage and causal loss of employment
    to be established and allows oral or written evidence, while rejecting reliance on unchallenged newspaper
    reports.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA public report of a dispute does not establish its effect
    on a particular claimant. Evidence from the claimant and employer, the exceptions and the correct
    benefit scope remain necessary. The project does not decide disputed facts, merits or entitlement.\n\
    \n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 32012, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n- [DMG 32015, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n- [DMG 32007, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch32`: PDF SHA-256 `5db1b5b8f473bf748cdbe42d45b23d48a5838c583013e1a554454644e2b5dbdb`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `a1dc36fa3d3513b1c9d7218f10c80a1417cd76cbe718b88baa3d57c6806de15b`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly contrasts relevant oral or written evidence with unchallenged
      newspaper reports.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0011
      quote: "32015   Evidence is usually in the form of oral or written statements from the claimant
        or the\n                                                                                  1\n\
        \        employer. The DM should not rely on unchallenged newspaper reports .\n              \
        \                                                                 1 R(U)6/61; R(U)11/63\n\n\n\n\
        \nVol 6 Amendment 14 October 2004"
      locator: DMG 32015
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-trade-dispute
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The evidential chain supports the trade-dispute question, which has express
      exceptions rather than automatic exclusion.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0010
      quote: "32012   Before deciding whether the claimant has lost employment because of a stoppage of\n\
        \        work caused by a TD the DM must establish\n\n        1.    the claimant's place of work
        (see DMG 32016 - 32057) and\n\n        2.    that there was a TD at the place of work and\n\n\
        \        3.    that there was a stoppage of work at the place of work and\n\n        4.    that
        the stoppage was due to the TD and\n\n        5.    that the claimant lost employment because
        of the stoppage of work.\n\n\n\n\nVol 6 Amendment 14 October 2004"
      locator: DMG 32012
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0009
      quote: "32006   The TD provisions do not apply if claimants can show that during the stoppage of\n\
        \             1\n        work they\n\n        1.       start work somewhere else (see DMG 32252
        - 32260) or\n                                                2\n        2.       have been made
        redundant (see DMG 32264 - 32265) or\n\n        3.       have returned to work for their employer
        but have then left for reasons other\n                 than the TD (see DMG 32266 -32274) or\n\
        \                                                               3\n        4.       are not directly
        interested in the dispute (see DMG 32201 - 32222).\n                                         \
        \                1 s 14(3); 2 ER Act 96, s 139(1) & (2); 3 JS Act 95, s 14(1)"
      locator: DMG 32006
